# Shared Mailbox Creation Lab

**Tenant:** `401ops.onmicrosoft.com`
**Date:** 2026-10-25
**Role used:** Global Administrator / Exchange Administrator
**Method:** Microsoft 365 admin center (GUI)



## Objective

Create a shared mailbox in Exchange Online and delegate access to an
existing licensed user, with no additional license consumed.

## Prerequisites Verified

- Entra ID tenant with Microsoft 365 Business Premium subscription
- Exchange Online organization initialized (confirmed via existing
  `UserMailbox`: `ChristyMarquez@401ops.onmicrosoft.com`)
- Admin role assigned to the acting account

## Steps Performed

1. Navigated to **admin.exchange.microsoft.com → Recipients → Mailboxes**.
   Note: shared mailbox *creation* has been removed from the EAC; only
   management actions (delegation, hide from address list, convert) remain.
2. Redirected to **admin.microsoft.com → Teams & groups → Shared mailboxes**.
3. Selected **Add a shared mailbox**.
4. Completed the form:

   | Field | Value |
   |---|---|
   | Display name | Support Desk |
   | Email address | supportdesk@401ops.onmicrosoft.com |

5. Confirmed creation — success banner returned: *"Your shared mailbox was created."*
6. Opened the new mailbox → **Members** → added `Christy Marquez`.

## Result

![Shared mailbox created successfully](docs/shared-mailbox-created.png)

The mailbox now appears in the **Shared mailboxes** list and replicates into
the delegate's Outlook/OWA within 15–60 minutes.

## Permissions Granted by Membership

Adding a member via this wizard assigns two permissions automatically:

- **FullAccess** — read, send, move, and delete items in the mailbox
- **SendAs** — outbound messages appear to originate from the shared address,
  not the individual delegate

No `SendOnBehalf` is granted by default. That must be applied separately if
"on behalf of" semantics are required.

## Verification Checklist

- [ ] Shared mailbox visible in M365 admin center list
- [ ] Shared mailbox visible in EAC with `RecipientTypeDetails = SharedMailbox`
- [ ] Delegate sees mailbox under **Shared mailboxes** in OWA after replication
- [ ] Delegate can compose using **From → Support Desk**
- [ ] Sent item lands in the shared mailbox's **Sent Items**, not the delegate's

## Key Takeaways

- Shared mailboxes are **unlicensed** up to 50 GB. No license is consumed on
  creation or through delegation.
- The **delegate** must have their own Exchange mailbox. A bare cloud-only
  user object cannot be delegated.
- Permission changes are **not instant**. Replication lag is the most common
  cause of "I added them but they can't see it yet" tickets.
- `-AutoMapping $true` (default) pushes the mailbox into the delegate's
  profile. For users with many shared mailboxes, disable auto-mapping to
  avoid slow Outlook startup.

## Equivalent PowerShell

```powershell
Connect-ExchangeOnline

New-Mailbox -Shared -Name "Support Desk" `
            -DisplayName "Support Desk" `
            -Alias supportdesk `
            -PrimarySmtpAddress supportdesk@401ops.onmicrosoft.com

Add-MailboxPermission -Identity supportdesk@401ops.onmicrosoft.com `
                      -User ChristyMarquez@401ops.onmicrosoft.com `
                      -AccessRights FullAccess -AutoMapping $true

Add-RecipientPermission -Identity supportdesk@401ops.onmicrosoft.com `
                        -Trustee ChristyMarquez@401ops.onmicrosoft.com `
                        -AccessRights SendAs
